{"action":"add_fourgram_ve_fixed","cost_tier":"light","description":"Add 4-gram value embeddings at 256x on top of the SOTA, RE-MEASURED on fixed code. The prior 4-gram results are retracted: fourgram_gate was never initialized under meta+to_empty, so the 4-gram signal was injected through a random gate. This configuration previously OOM'd (~151GB); it is now feasible because NGRAM_STATE_ROWWISE removes ~21GB of optimizer state and NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD removes the dense embedding gradients. Unlike the PK memory, this needs no learned routing -- it is a direct hash lookup of the same form as the bigram/trigram VEs that actually won.","duration":{"type":"full_run"},"fingerprint":"94bc389e9b3c2b67","implementation":{"entrypoint":"train.py env NGRAM_TABLE_MULT + NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT","test":"tests/test_baseline_training_spec.py"},"intervention_id":"int_sota_fourgram256_fixed","name":"SOTA + 4-gram VE @256x (on FIXED gate init)","parameters":{"env":{"DOC_MASK":"1","DOC_MASK_MODE":"seg","NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT":"256","NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD":"1","NGRAM_STATE_ROWWISE":"1","NGRAM_TABLE_MULT":"256","WARMDOWN_RATIO":"0.75"}},"reversible":true,"safety":{"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss":true,"max_train_loss":100,"validation_policy_control":false,"vram_note":"256x (~57GB) + seg mask (negligible); fits."},"status":"available","tags":["ngram","fourgram","order","re_measure","explore"],"target":{"selector":"SOTA + NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT=256 (fixed gate init)","type":"model_architecture"},"timing":{"stage":"model_construction"},"version":1}
