{"action":"raise_base_capacity_with_fourgram","cost_tier":"light","description":"Raise the BASE bigram/trigram capacity 256->384 on SOTA #4 (which now includes 4-gram@256x). The base-capacity ladder was measured BEFORE the 4-gram order existed (and while the fourgram gate was broken), giving -0.000611 sub-threshold. This tests the INTERACTION: with 4-gram carrying part of the rare-context load, does extra base capacity become more useful, less useful, or unchanged?","duration":{"type":"full_run"},"fingerprint":"309e08d3d8dd9d53","implementation":{"entrypoint":"train.py env NGRAM_TABLE_MULT + NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT","test":"tests/test_baseline_training_spec.py"},"intervention_id":"int_sota004_base384","name":"SOTA #4 with base capacity 384x","parameters":{"env":{"DOC_MASK":"1","DOC_MASK_MODE":"seg","NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT":"256","NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD":"1","NGRAM_STATE_ROWWISE":"1","NGRAM_TABLE_MULT":"384","WARMDOWN_RATIO":"0.75"}},"reversible":true,"safety":{"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss":true,"max_train_loss":100,"validation_policy_control":false,"vram_note":"256x (~57GB) + seg mask (negligible); fits."},"status":"available","tags":["ngram","capacity","interaction","explore"],"target":{"selector":"SOTA #4 + NGRAM_TABLE_MULT=384","type":"model_architecture"},"timing":{"stage":"model_construction"},"version":1}
{"action":"add_fivegram_order","cost_tier":"light","description":"Add 5-gram value embeddings @256x on top of SOTA #4 (which already has bigram+trigram@256x and 4-gram@256x). Tests whether the n-gram ORDER ladder continues past 4-gram. The 4-gram rung paid -0.001307 (6/6 hold-out seeds); capacity is closed on every axis tested, so order is the only remaining direction. Newly implemented as EXPLORE:NGRAM_FIVEGRAM -- verified byte-identical when off (20 capture sites / 76588.1MB, matching the pre-change baseline) and verified working when on (26 capture sites / 87.2GB). fivegram_gate is zero-initialised (independently checked at init_weights 743-744), avoiding the uninitialised-gate defect that produced a campaign-long false negative for 4-gram.","duration":{"type":"full_run"},"fingerprint":"4d575332fbdb8ebd","implementation":{"entrypoint":"train.py env NGRAM_TABLE_MULT + NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT","test":"tests/test_baseline_training_spec.py"},"intervention_id":"int_sota004_fivegram256","name":"SOTA #4 + 5-gram VE @256x","parameters":{"env":{"DOC_MASK":"1","DOC_MASK_MODE":"seg","NGRAM_FIVEGRAM_MULT":"256","NGRAM_FOURGRAM_MULT":"256","NGRAM_SPARSE_GRAD":"1","NGRAM_STATE_ROWWISE":"1","NGRAM_TABLE_MULT":"256","WARMDOWN_RATIO":"0.75"}},"reversible":true,"safety":{"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss":true,"max_train_loss":100,"validation_policy_control":false,"vram_note":"256x (~57GB) + seg mask (negligible); fits."},"status":"available","tags":["ngram","fivegram","order","explore"],"target":{"selector":"SOTA #4 + NGRAM_FIVEGRAM_MULT=256","type":"model_architecture"},"timing":{"stage":"model_construction"},"version":1}
