{"action": "reduce_transformer_depth_and_width_to_land_below_the_repetition_cliff", "cost_tier": "moderate", "description": "The campaign's one real effect. Depth 6 at dim 640 raises throughput enough to consume 483M tokens (1.9 passes) in the 300s budget, landing in the grid cell between the baseline and the 2.3-pass repetition cliff. MATRIX_LR 0.03 is the Muon basin floor re-derived at this shape. Measured against int_baseline_frozen at n=97 paired seeds: -0.002431, 91/97 better, t=-15.62, 0.93 gates. Real, precisely determined, and below the 0.002614 adoption floor. NOT ADOPTED.", "duration": {"type": "full_run"}, "fingerprint": "9c947d3eaa052539", "implementation": {"entrypoint": "train.py: DEPTH and MODEL_DIM env gates in build_model_config", "test": "RESOLVED_CONFIG echo asserts depth/dim; MODEL_DIM must be a multiple of HEAD_DIM=128"}, "intervention_id": "int_depth6_dim640", "name": "Depth 6 at dim 640 with Muon MATRIX_LR 0.03", "parameters": {"env": {"ATTN_BACKEND": "fa3", "COMPILE_MODE": "max-autotune-no-cudagraphs", "DEPTH": "6", "DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE": "72", "MATRIX_LR": "0.03", "MODEL_DIM": "640", "STOP_MODE": "time", "TIME_BUDGET": "300", "TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE": "147456", "WINDOW_PATTERN": "TTTL"}}, "reversible": true, "safety": {"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss": true, "max_train_loss": 100, "one_compiled_graph_required": true}, "status": "unit_tested", "tags": ["depth", "boundary_optimum", "n97", "not_adopted"], "target": {"selector": "transformer block count and residual width", "type": "model_shape"}, "timing": {"stage": "full_run_configuration"}, "version": 1}
{"action": "increase_unique_token_count_so_throughput_no_longer_buys_repetition", "cost_tier": "moderate", "description": "N1. Raise the unique-token pool from ~250M to ~750M so that raising throughput buys NEW tokens instead of additional passes. Decouples the two quantities the frame currently confounds. NOTE: this changes the scope key -- the ten frozen shards are part of the registered frame -- so it defines a NEW frame rather than an experiment inside walltime_5min_h200. Recorded here because it is the campaign's highest-value untested prediction, not because it is runnable as-is.", "duration": {"type": "full_run"}, "fingerprint": "01983fe2f845f0e1", "implementation": {"entrypoint": "NOT IMPLEMENTED -- requires a new registered decision frame and a new noise floor", "test": "token-law fit R^2 out to 2x the current budget; cliff must not appear at 2.3 passes"}, "intervention_id": "int_unfrozen_corpus_3x", "name": "Three-times-larger unique corpus at fixed budget", "parameters": {"env": {"ATTN_BACKEND": "fa3", "COMPILE_MODE": "max-autotune-no-cudagraphs", "DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE": "72", "NUM_SHARDS": "30", "STOP_MODE": "time", "TIME_BUDGET": "300", "TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE": "147456", "WINDOW_PATTERN": "TTTL"}}, "reversible": true, "safety": {"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss": true, "max_train_loss": 100, "one_compiled_graph_required": true}, "status": "proposed", "tags": ["n1", "data", "out_of_frame", "highest_value"], "target": {"selector": "training shard set", "type": "data_source"}, "timing": {"stage": "full_run_configuration"}, "version": 1}
{"action": "apply_weight_decay_only_to_ngram_rows_below_a_visit_frequency_threshold", "cost_tier": "moderate", "description": "N2. Uniform table decay closes 93% of the train/val gap and still degrades the endpoint, because a norm penalty cannot distinguish a rare-key memorisation from a frequent-key statistic. Visit count can: it is already computed every step as part of the gather. Decay rows below threshold c* only. The discriminating signature is an INTERIOR optimum in c* -- a monotone curve means the count signal is inert and this is just weaker uniform decay.", "duration": {"type": "full_run"}, "fingerprint": "9149d6fb6729b045", "implementation": {"entrypoint": "NOT IMPLEMENTED -- needs a per-row visit counter alongside the n-gram gather", "test": "c* sweep must show an interior optimum; winner re-measured at n=10 on disjoint seeds"}, "intervention_id": "int_ngram_count_conditioned_decay", "name": "Visit-count-conditioned decay on hashed n-gram rows", "parameters": {"env": {"ATTN_BACKEND": "fa3", "COMPILE_MODE": "max-autotune-no-cudagraphs", "DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE": "72", "NGRAM_WD_COUNT_THRESHOLD": "8", "NGRAM_WD_LAMBDA": "0.1", "STOP_MODE": "time", "TIME_BUDGET": "300", "TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE": "147456", "WINDOW_PATTERN": "TTTL"}}, "reversible": true, "safety": {"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss": true, "max_train_loss": 100, "one_compiled_graph_required": true}, "status": "proposed", "tags": ["n2", "ngram", "regularization", "last_surviving_member"], "target": {"selector": "hashed n-gram value-embedding rows, gated on per-row visit count", "type": "regularizer"}, "timing": {"stage": "full_run_configuration"}, "version": 1}
{"action": "sample_the_label_offset_once_per_sequence_instead_of_once_per_token", "cost_tier": "moderate", "description": "N3. Our per-token instantiation was null, but per-token sampling makes the target a mixture over offsets and the Bayes-optimal output a blur -- a specification error on our side, not a refutation of the method. Drawn once per sequence the offset is inferable from context and the target stays identifiable. Label-only augmentation is the ENTIRE admissible set here: masking and permutation change token IDs, which change the n-gram hash keys that are 96.8% of the model.", "duration": {"type": "full_run"}, "fingerprint": "858db64404508b73", "implementation": {"entrypoint": "train.py: _offset_targets(y, gen) -- currently per-token; needs a per-sequence draw", "test": "per-sequence must be flat in T over {2,4} where per-token degrades monotonically"}, "intervention_id": "int_offset_aug_per_sequence", "name": "Label-offset augmentation with the offset drawn per sequence", "parameters": {"env": {"ATTN_BACKEND": "fa3", "COMPILE_MODE": "max-autotune-no-cudagraphs", "DEVICE_BATCH_SIZE": "72", "OFFSET_AUG": "1", "OFFSET_AUG_SCOPE": "sequence", "OFFSET_AUG_T": "2", "STOP_MODE": "time", "TIME_BUDGET": "300", "TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE": "147456", "WINDOW_PATTERN": "TTTL"}}, "reversible": true, "safety": {"fast_fail_nonfinite_loss": true, "max_train_loss": 100, "one_compiled_graph_required": true}, "status": "proposed", "tags": ["n3", "augmentation", "untested_not_refuted"], "target": {"selector": "training labels only; inputs and n-gram hashes untouched", "type": "target_transform"}, "timing": {"stage": "full_run_configuration"}, "version": 1}
